=== ANSWER A ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git log --since=2026-03-29T00:00:00 --until=2026-04-13 --format='%h|%an|%ae|%ad|%s' --date=iso; echo; git log -1 --format='%ad' --date=iso
 - Bash: git log --format='%an|%ae' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20; echo; for f in $(git ls-files); do git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 -w --line-porcelain -- $f 2>/dev/null | grep -a '^author ' ; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20
 - Bash: for f in $(git ls-files); do git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 -w --line-porcelain -- $f 2>/dev/null | grep -a '^author-mail ' ; done | grep -E 'troy|vansh' | sort | uniq -c
FINAL ANSWER:
Two people committed in the 14 days up to 2026-04-12 (window starts 2026-03-29), after setting aside the formatting commit and bots.

| Person | Commits in window | Lines still in the code |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | `02afce3` test: vary header coverage; `b2005d9` lib: annotate handlers | 746 |
| Vansh Sharma | `5317ebe` docs: app.del() with app.delete() in README example (#411) | 1 |

- **Troy Goode:** Troy appears under two emails, `troy@laptop.example` and `<email redacted>`. I counted them as one person. The two window commits use the laptop address. The 746 lines are 48 under the laptop address and 698 under the gmail address.
- **Vansh Sharma:** the one remaining line is the README fix.
- **Excluded:** `62628c0`, Fiona Formatter's reformat commit, which only changed indentation and quotes. Dependabot's most recent commit is `ee714bd`, which falls before the window.
- **Line counts:** I used `git blame` with `62628c0` ignored, so reformatted lines still credit their original author. Lines count for a person if they wrote them at any time, not only in the window.

=== ANSWER B ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Skill: {"skill": "tool:skill", "args": "--team"}
 - Bash: git log --no-merges --since="2026-03-29" --until="2026-04-13" --pretty=format:"%h|%an|%ae|%ad|%s" --date=short; echo; git log -1 --format=%ad --date=iso
 - Bash: for c in b2005d9 02afce3 5317ebe; do echo "== $c"; git show --stat --format= $c; done
echo ---; for f in $(git ls-files); do git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 -w --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^(author|boundary)? ?' | grep '^author ' ; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn
 - Bash: for f in $(git ls-files); do git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 --line-porcelain -- "$f" | grep -E '^[0-9a-f]{40} ' | cut -c1-7; done | sort | uniq -c | grep -E 'b2005d9|02afce3|5317ebe'
echo ---no-ignore; for f in $(git ls-files); do git blame --line-porcelain -- "$f" | grep -E '^[0-9a-f]{40} ' | cut -c1-7; done | sort | uniq -c | grep -E 'b2005d9|02afce3|5317ebe|62628c0'
FINAL ANSWER:
Two people committed in the 14 days up to 2026-04-12 (the window is 2026-03-29 to 2026-04-12), once the formatting-only commit is set aside. The skill's own commands use `--since` relative to today (2026-10-24), so I used explicit dates instead. `--team` normally launches the contributor-analyzer agent, but this window has only four commits, so I read the log and blame directly.

| Person | Commits in window | Lines still in the code today |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 2 (`b2005d9` lib: annotate handlers, 2026-04-10; `02afce3` test: vary header coverage, 2026-04-10) | 47 (36 from `02afce3`, 11 from `b2005d9`) |
| Vansh Sharma | 1 (`5317ebe` docs: `app.del()` → `app.delete()` in README, #411, 2026-04-07) | 1 |

- **Excluded as formatting-only:** `62628c0` by Fiona Formatter (2026-04-12) reformatted the JS to 4-space indent and double quotes. She has no other commits in the window, so she doesn't appear.
- **Bots:** none committed in the window. The dependabot commit `ee714bd` falls before 2026-03-29.
- **Counted once:** Troy Goode appears under a single name and email across both commits.

**How I counted surviving lines:** I ran `git blame` with `--ignore-rev 62628c0`, so the reformat doesn't take credit for lines it only restyled. The count is the lines still attributed to each commit.

Without that flag, the reformat takes 11 of Troy's 12 `lib/index.js` lines, leaving 1 for `b2005d9`. His survivors would then be 37 instead of 47. His tests and Vansh's README line are unaffected either way.

